  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 3e4b5683c1ea36345958694d590b6436, type: 3}
  m_Name: COC3_Quiz_LO3_Testing_Q04
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::QuizQuestionData
  questionText: Folder redirection points Documents at a path on the server. Why
    must that path be a network path and not a local one?
  choices:
  - Local paths are slower to open
  - Windows blocks local paths in Group Policy
  - 'The client''s C: drive is not the server''s C: drive'
  - A local path cannot contain a user name
  correctChoiceIndex: 2
  points: 10
  explanation: A local path would redirect every user to a folder on their own machine,
    which is the opposite of what redirection is for.
